spans.s:
तिरय् तिर˚यति veil, cover, hide;
 restrain, oppress;
pervade, fill.

तिर॑स् prep. through, across, beyond, past, without, against
(acc.), apart, secretly, or safely from (abl.);
 adv. crossways, aside,
awry;
 privately, covertly. — Cf. कृ, धा, भू.

तिरो॑अह्न्य a. having lasted beyond a day;
 left from
the day before yesterday.

तिर्यग्योनि f. the womb of an animal;
 condition or race
of animals (incl. plants), organic nature.

तीर्थ॑ n. (m.) passage, access, approach (esp. to a water
or the altar);
 descent into a water, landing or bathing-place (poss.
˚वन्त्†), shrine or holy place of pilgrimage, any venerable or worthy
thing or person, esp. counsellor, adviser, teacher (also counsel,
instruction);
 certain lines or parts of the hand sacred to sev. gods;
the right way, place, or moment.

तीर्थक a. worthy, sacred. m. an ascetic, the chief of a
sect;
 n. a holy bathing-place.

तीर्थकर a. creating a passage, sc. through life
(Viṣṇu & Śiva);
 m. a venerable person, esp. the chief of a sect.

ती॑र्थ्य a. belonging to a ford or bathing-place;
 m. =
तीर्थक m.
